  "rewrites": {
   "4": {
    "original": "There are small concerns, particularly in attack where prolific centre-forward Robin van Persie is coming off the back of an awkward challenge that led to a thigh muscle injury.There is still the question of how manager David Moyes lines up ahead of the game and if Rooney's injury provides an opportunity for the Dutchman to make a right-footed cameo instead of bringing him on after an hour, which is the plan he may adopt on Sunday.",
    "rewrite": "There are some minor worries, especially in attack, as prolific center-forward Robin van Persie recovers from a muscle injury resulting from a challenging tackle. There remains uncertainty about how manager David Moyes will set his lineup before the match, and whether Rooney's absence offers van Persie a chance to appear for a few minutes with his right foot, rather than substituting him after an hour, which is currently the planned strategy for Sunday."
   },
   "15": {
    "original": "Shaky and stodgy early-season City strugglers recently returned to Leeds' former symbolic and geographical centre and used an ageless touch of class to rustle maximum points from a 1-0 victory.",
    "rewrite": "Shaky and solid early-season City performers recently ventured back to the heart of Leeds' historical and physical center and deployed time-honored skill to secure three points with a 1-0 win."
   },
   "16": {
    "original": "They now plot their third away test of the campaign at Burnley in Dyche's first Old Trafford meeting.",
    "rewrite": "They will now face Burnley in an away test match for the third time during the campaign, marking Dyche's first encounter at Old Trafford."
   },
   "5": {
    "original": "Certain it has to be much better, there are few doubting it this time though.",
    "rewrite": "There is little doubt this time, as it is certain to be much better."
   }
